{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794910622,"nonce":"lsL6C2tVL6Mbmzs8l3jkHt/F82M=","message":"Implemented locally across x-idl, xwindow, hxn-window, hxn and hxn-gpu; no commits, pushes or publications made.\n\nhxn-window reuses xwindow's browser wire protocol and DOM agent. x-idl accepts the hxn host-agent entry point, and the backend supports synchronous dispatch for unthreaded Emscripten while retaining its mailbox path. Ash uses its wasm build/page tooling and host-agent import; threaded Emscripten starts the same agent on the page; unthreaded Emscripten dispatches directly and returns to the event loop. Missing browser hosts become normal Haxe exceptions. The plain Rust library does not select a runtime with cargo features.\n\nThe browser canvas supplies size/DPI, focus, visibility, keyboard, pointer, mouse, wheel, touch, IME and gamepad events through the existing API. xwindow-gamepad's native gilrs Hub is excluded from wasm; browser controllers remain enabled through the DOM agent and xwindow_core::gamepad. hxn-gpu's present example now opens an hxn-window window, uses its physical size and resize events, and maps its browser handle to Canvas. GPU rendering retains ownership of the drawing buffer.\n\nInstalled haxelibs provide hxn window doctor and hxn window check through the CLI extension protocol tracked in 54620d2dbe2191c8ff1f85fae480f5e383e06fef2a62335bdf3fb7dcbeb12abd. The package includes the tool, native/browser checks and page assets; no repository shell helper is the public workflow. Source before-check/build hooks regenerate the shared page modules. README, skills and browser/release workflows reflect this design.\n\nValidation: native hxn-window checks passed on Ash hybrid/JIT/interpreter, hxcpp and CPPIA. Browser event checks passed repeatedly on Ash wasm, unthreaded Emscripten and threaded Emscripten, including controlled gamepad and IME events. Both WebGPU and WebGL2 present/readback passed in all three modes. Unavailable browser hosts were rejected through Haxe under Node with both Emscripten variants. The x-idl and xwindow tests and generated page-agent tests passed. The hxn runtime matrix and mobile validation are recorded in the CLI extension issue. Physical gamepad/real IME interaction and Windows/Linux CI have not been verified by these local runs.\n\nRemaining integration: commit the sibling changes and update Git revision pins, then coordinate the hxn CLI/haxelib and hxn-window releases. Current released hxn 0.3.6 has no extension protocol and released hxn-window 0.2.0 has no wasm archives; workflow version references must follow those releases. The GPU browser workflow now links hxn-window for present, but its setup's pinned window release must also advance. Local validation uses ignored sibling path patches. Keep this issue open until those dependency and CI steps are complete. Mixed-profile threaded Emscripten runtime-symbol collisions remain separately tracked in cc8ef3127222f5aa6ebea486022642c5452ab0fcd326077252441d46886a586d; matching release-profile packages link and pass.","files":null}]}